<title>SUDAN: Sudan's Bashir to take fighting charges to OAU.</title>
<headline>Sudan's Bashir to take fighting charges to OAU.</headline>
<dateline>KHARTOUM 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sudanese President Omar Hassan al-Bashir would complain at an African summit about fighting in Sudan which he blames on Ethiopia, Uganda and Eritrea.</p>
<p>State-run radio said Bashir, who headed on Tuesday to the Organisation of African Unity (OAU) summit on civil war in Zaire, would deliver a speech charging the three with fighting alongside rebels who want to topple the Khartoum government.</p>
<p>Ethiopia, Eritrea and Uganda have denied any involvement in the clashes in Sudan which began in January.</p>
<p>Foreign Minister Ali Osman Mohamed Taha will also attend the summit due to open in Togo on Wednesday to agree ways of brokering peace in Zaire's civil war.</p>
</text>
